# What this backend's rig is, told to bin/test and through it to the suite.
#
# Sourced by bin/test, which exports whatever is assigned here and reads MATRIX_APIS to decide which
# of the suite it can run. Every entry keeps a value which is already set, so one given on the
# command line wins:
#
#   MATRIX_ACCOUNTS=login bin/test --backend tuwunel

# The APIs this rig serves, which is the client-server API alone.
#
# The identity, push gateway and application service APIs are each served by a server of its own and
# this rig runs none of them; tuwunel.toml turns federation off, which leaves the server-server API
# with nothing to answer. Asking for one of those here is a run of nothing, said rather than failed.
MATRIX_APIS="${MATRIX_APIS:-client-server}"

# How the suite gets an account. Tuwunel has no way to accept any password, so this rig opens
# registration instead and the account is registered before it is logged into.
MATRIX_ACCOUNTS="${MATRIX_ACCOUNTS:-register}"

# No authorization server, which is how the suite is told to leave the OAuth 2.0 flow out: those
# operations are answered by a homeserver which delegates authentication, and the rig in `synapse/`
# is the only one which runs one.
MATRIX_OAUTH_HOMESERVER="${MATRIX_OAUTH_HOMESERVER-}"
